// STATUS: NON-CERTIFIED SCHEMATIC SPECIFICATION / LEGACY STUB (QUARANTINED)
// Not kernel-certified. Carries zero proof-discharge authority.
// Alignment notes against paper-en/paper.tex §10:
//   - Pre-localization adjunction `ε ⊣ α` is strictly asymmetric: counit
//     `(id_F, ι) : ε(F) -> E` and retraction `(id_F, r) : E -> ε(F)` are
//     distinct 1-morphisms; internal reflector unit `η_r` is not invertible in E.
//   - `thm:ac-oc-duality` is CONDITIONAL on existence, descent, and coherence
//     of localizations (no unbounded-depth lift).
//   - The former equation `Con(F ∪ E) = Con(F) = Con(ZFC + 2-inacc)` is
//     WITHDRAWN (`cor:ac-oc-conservativity` is conditional definitional
//     conservativity only).
//   - `def:SSE` and `lem:SS-membership-E` do NOT invoke Lambek-Scott for a
//     left adjoint to `ev_M` or cocomplete AFT for a left reflector.
//   - `def:level6-cE` (`\tilde{F}_S`) requires explicit faithful relative
//     interpretations `F -> F' -> S`, and `thm:dual-afnt` covers both the
//     slice-conservative retraction branch and the diagonal branch via `ε(T_S)`.
//   - `ensures false` declarations below depend on unproved stdlib axioms.
// Only `proofs/ss-membership/{witness.vr, formal.vr}` (representation-level
// union introduction A -> A \/ B \/ C) has an independently replayed native
// kernel certificate.
// =============================================================================
// MSFS §10 — AC/OC Duality and Dual Boundary Lemma (schematic stubs)
// =============================================================================

